Title: POLITICIAN
Credit: written by
Author: Leonard Menchiari
Draft date: 2026-11-10 (shooting script, draft 3)

/* File: stories/politician/screenplay.fountain
   Draft 3: Leonard's 22 comments on draft 2 applied (idea.md), plus the Braintrust fixes listed in chat.
   Shot notes: [[SHOT | seconds | size and angle | movement | note]]. Scene ids S01..S10, shot ids per scene.
   ASSUMPTION (no answer yet, Claude's pick): bobblehead not gold, hand on heart; the gun moment plays in his head; the helicopter holds high and far, unheard under the crowd until the first crack.
   PROPOSED: the final line; bearer bonds; the scope with face boxes; Walther PPK/S.
   Accents: everyone in the town and on the news speaks English with strong accents nobody can place. The old man is American, with a slight accent. */

.EXT. CITIES AROUND THE WORLD - DAY TO SUNSET #S01#

[[SH010 | 3 | WIDE, high | Handheld, phone-camera feel | Riots open the film (Leonard). Different cities, different countries]]

A crowd fills an avenue from wall to wall. Above the heads, signs with the same old face: devil horns drawn on, the eyes crossed out in red, one printout of him photoshopped hanging from a noose.

NEWS ANCHORS (V.O.)
(overlapping, many accents)
...protests in more than forty countries... ...the index lost another eleven percent... ...fuel up again overnight...

[[SH020 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]

A cardboard sign. His face. A red X over each eye.

[[SH030 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | Numbers per liter, no currency sign. Set up for the last line]]

Another country. A gas station. A worker on a ladder pulls 1.94 off the price board and slides in 5.89. Under it, DIESEL: 2.07 becomes 6.31. A line of cars behind him. Nobody honks.

[[SH040 | 2 | WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | ]]

Another country. A highway out of a city, jammed. Mattresses tied on car roofs. Children's faces at the windows.

[[SH050 | 4 | WIDE, long lens | Handheld | Distance: nothing explicit]]

A police line. Hands pull a POLICEMAN into the crowd by his vest. Another officer drags him back. A pistol rises above the heads and fires. The police fire back. Everyone scatters.

[[SH060 | 3 | MEDIUM WIDE | Handheld | Leonard: riot shields struck]]

A wall of riot shields. A bottle of fire bursts against it. Flames run down the shields and over the boots. The line breaks.

[[SH070 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | Leonard: the truck, realistic]]

A police truck stands abandoned, windows smashed. A bottle sails through the broken windshield. Fire fills the cab.

[[SH080 | 2 | EXTREME WIDE | Slow pan | ]]

Sunset. A skyline under columns of smoke. Sirens far away.

[[SH090 | 9 | MEDIUM, a TV in a shop window | Locked-off | Leonard: seen on a screen, professional news logos. His clean face on screen]]

A television behind a cracked shop window. A news channel: a polished logo, a red BREAKING bar, a ticker of red numbers. In the corner, his official portrait: the same old face, clean, smiling. A REPORTER, sexy, every hair in place, on a rooftop with smoke behind her.

REPORTER
His location is still unknown. Authorities are warning the locals that any harm to this man will have serious repercussions.

SMASH CUT TO:

.EXT. DIRT ROAD INTO A TOWN - DAY #S02#

[[SH010 | 2 | EXTREME WIDE | Locked-off | Hard cut to silence]]

Silence. The sun on the rooftops of a dry, dusty town.

[[SH020 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | Leonard: stray dog]]

A stray dog lies in the shadow of an abandoned building, on the edge of a crumbled concrete wall. Heat rises off the ground.

[[SH030 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | ]]

Far out on a dirt road, a car comes out of the heat shimmer at full speed, a plume of dust behind it.

[[SH040 | 2 | LOW, ground level | Locked-off, car passes over camera | The speeding car (Leonard)]]

The car tears over the camera.

[[SH050 | 2 | INSERT, ground level | Locked-off | ]]

A front wheel locks and slides through the dirt to a rough stop. Dust rolls past.

[[SH060 | 2 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | Leonard: separate shot]]

The dog lifts its head.

[[SH070 | 4 | MEDIUM, through the windshield | Locked-off | ]]

The OLD MAN behind the wheel, American, his shirt dark with sweat, slowly raises his head and looks ahead, frightened.

[[SH080 | 2 | INSERT, dashboard | Locked-off | Leonard: separate shot. ASSUMPTION: not gold, no thumb up (no Trump)]]

A painted bobblehead on the dashboard: him, smiling, a hand on his heart. Nodding.

[[SH090 | 2 | INSERT, passenger seat | Locked-off | Leonard: separate shot]]

A BRIEFCASE on the passenger seat, papers sticking out of it, shut in a hurry.

[[SH100 | 3 | POV | Dolly zoom | Vertigo effect (Leonard)]]

The dirt road runs straight into the town. It stretches away from him.

[[SH110 | 2 | CLOSE, through the windshield, beside the bobblehead | Locked-off | Leonard: old-school, static]]

He looks left.

[[SH120 | 2 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]

Broken ground and a dry ditch. No road.

[[SH130 | 2 | CLOSE, same frame | Locked-off | ]]

He looks right.

[[SH140 | 2 | WIDE | Locked-off | Leonard: the only way is through]]

Rubble, then the town itself, its buildings running to the horizon. No road.

[[SH150 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]

The rear-view mirror. An empty road. Nobody.

[[SH160 | 2 | CLOSE, same frame | Locked-off | ]]

He looks down at the dashboard.

[[SH170 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]

The fuel needle rests on the edge of E.

[[SH180 | 2 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]

Sweat runs down his temple. He breathes in.

[[SH190 | 2 | INSERT, footwell | Locked-off | Leonard: the accelerator]]

His shoe presses the accelerator, gently.

.EXT. TOWN - MAIN STREET - DAY #S03#

[[SH010 | 5 | WIDE, side view | Dolly alongside the car, long lens, flat | Leonard: we dolly with the car as it moves through the town]]

The car crawls through the town. Tall, cheap apartment blocks slide past behind it, laundry on the balconies. Nobody outside. From open windows the same news echoes from television to television.

[[SH020 | 8 | MEDIUM, passenger side | Locked-off | ]]

He glances at the briefcase.

OLD MAN
We'll get there, don't worry... Wait till they see what I was able to-- what--? No, no no no...

The engine pops.

[[SH030 | 2 | GROUND LEVEL | Locked-off | Leonard]]

A front wheel rolls toward the camera and stops right in front of it.

[[SH040 | 3 | INSERT, dashboard | Locked-off | Leonard: separate insert]]

A beep. The fuel light blinks. His hand twists the key. The engine dies with a last clap.

[[SH050 | 4 | EXTREME WIDE, high | Locked-off | Leonard: alone in a large empty crossroads. The car stays here until the end]]

The car sits alone in the middle of a large, empty crossroads. The clap echoes off the buildings and fades.

[[SH060 | 4 | MEDIUM CLOSE | Handheld, gentle | ]]

OLD MAN
Not here, no...

He peeks around. Empty. He takes the briefcase and gets out, leaving the door open.

.EXT. TOWN - SIDE STREETS - DAY #S04#

[[SH010 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld, tracking beside him | We stay with him (Leonard, Q12)]]

He walks fast, the briefcase against his chest, trying not to make a sound. His breath gets heavier.

[[SH020 | 2 | POV | Handheld | ]]

A doorway. A bead curtain sways.

[[SH030 | 2 | POV | Handheld | ]]

A window. A television glows. An old woman eating turns her head toward the street.

[[SH040 | 3 | MEDIUM WIDE | Handheld | Leonard: he feels recognized and runs]]

On his left, a small group of people at a doorway. One of them looks at him. Looks again. Nudges the man next to him. The old man walks faster. Then he runs.

[[SH050 | 2 | MEDIUM | Handheld | ]]

He turns a corner and slams into a big, robust FAT PERSON.

[[SH060 | 2 | WIDE | Locked-off | Leonard: shot of the fall]]

He bounces off the big body and lands flat on his back on the ground.

[[SH070 | 4 | LOW, from the ground | Handheld | Leonard: not sure yet]]

The fat person looks down at him. He can't place him. Then his eyes widen with excitement.

FAT PERSON
(a thick accent from nowhere you could name)
Hey... wait. Aren't you--

[[SH080 | 5 | CLOSE | Handheld | ]]

On the ground, the old man covers his face with his hand.

OLD MAN
I don't know who you think I am. I don't know you!

[[SH090 | 7 | MEDIUM | Handheld | Leonard: the friend films, then texts, in the background, during the line]]

FAT PERSON
It IS you. What are you doing here, all alone? Nobody around to baby-sit you?

Behind him, his FRIEND films the old man on his phone, then types fast with both thumbs.

[[SH100 | 5 | CLOSE TWO SHOT | Handheld, tight | His line restored]]

The fat person grabs him by the collar and hauls him up. He looks down at the briefcase in the old man's arms.

FAT PERSON
Is that what you like to do with our tax money?

[[SH110 | 6 | CLOSE | Handheld, tight | ]]

FAT PERSON
Give me one reason why I shouldn't rip your guts open right now, in front of everyone.

[[SH120 | 2 | WIDE, low | Locked-off | ]]

Above them, faces appear at the windows.

[[SH130 | 4 | MEDIUM | Handheld | Leonard: the friend's line]]

The old man shrinks and slides out of the grip. The fat person lets him go. The old man runs.

FRIEND
(in the background)
You let him get away?!

.EXT. TOWN - STREETS BACK TO THE CROSSROADS - CONTINUOUS #S05#

[[SH010 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld, backing in front of him | Variation in the voices]]

He runs. The buildings wake up. Someone bangs a pot on a balcony railing. A whistle.

VOICES
(from windows and balconies, overlapping)
Thief! / Close the street! / He's going to the crossroads!

[[SH020 | 3 | WIDE, long lens | Handheld | ]]

The friends run after him, and people pour out of doorways to join them.

[[SH030 | 2 | WIDE | Handheld, running | ]]

A whole crowd runs after him, faster than he is.

[[SH040 | 2 | MEDIUM | Handheld, running | Leonard: he trips]]

He trips. The briefcase hits the asphalt and bursts open.

[[SH050 | 3 | INSERT | Locked-off | Leonard: insert. PROPOSED: bearer bonds. Research item]]

Large engraved certificates spill out: PAY TO BEARER. ONE HUNDRED THOUSAND US DOLLARS.

[[SH060 | 3 | WIDE | Handheld | His decoy (Leonard, Part 1)]]

He looks at the crowd, then flings the open case toward them. The certificates fly. The front of the crowd drops to the ground, fighting over them.

[[SH070 | 3 | CLOSE | Handheld, running | ]]

VOICE (O.S.)
Don't let him get away!!!

He runs on, out into the crossroads, past his empty car, pulling out his phone.

[[SH080 | 4 | INSERT, his phone | Locked-off | Leonard: clear insert of the phone]]

His sweaty thumb slides across the lock screen. It fails. It works. A contact with no name, only a number. Call.

[[SH090 | 10 | CLOSE | Handheld, running | ]]

OLD MAN
(into the phone)
It's me! I have the money! The car broke down, I'm on foot, come get me, fast! I'm slightly south from where we were supposed to meet, the add--

[[SH100 | 2 | CLOSE | Handheld | ]]

A rock hits him between the phone and his ear.

[[SH110 | 3 | WIDE | Handheld | ELEMENT from here: old man beaten. Not exaggerated: he must still look cool at the end]]

He falls and rolls onto the sidewalk at the far corner of the crossroads. Blood runs down his face. His car stands in the middle of the crossroads behind him. The yelling closes in.

.EXT. CROSSROADS - CONTINUOUS #S06#

[[SH010 | 3 | LOW, his eye level on the ground | Handheld | Leonard: the crowd getting closer]]

Feet and faces fill the frame, closing in.

[[SH020 | 4 | MEDIUM, low | Locked-off | Gun: Walther PPK/S, nickel, 7 in the magazine + 1 chambered = 8 (checked). Shot 1 of 8]]

A gunshot. Everyone freezes. On the ground, he holds a small nickel pistol up at the sky.

OLD MAN
STAY BACK!!!

[[SH030 | 4 | MEDIUM | Handheld | ]]

He points it at the crowd. They take a step back.

OLD MAN
Don't get close! Go away!

[[SH040 | 4 | WIDE | Slow push in | His car in the middle of the crossroads]]

Some of them back away. The tough ones step forward. They don't run. They walk toward him, slowly, without fear.

[[SH050 | 7 | MEDIUM, his side | Handheld | Shots 2 to 7: six shots. Countdown audible between shots (Leonard). Distance on the falls]]

He shoots. A man drops. He shoots again. Another drops. The rest break into a sprint, twenty meters away. He keeps firing, counting down out loud between shots.

OLD MAN
...four... three... two...

[[SH060 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off | Shot 8 of 8: the magazine is now empty, he believes one is left]]

He fires once more.

OLD MAN
One.

[[SH070 | 6 | CLOSE, slow push in | Locked-off | ASSUMPTION: plays in his head. Leonard: more intense, the realization]]

The sound drains away until only his breathing is left. In front of him the sprinting crowd slows to a crawl. He looks at the faces. He looks at the gun. His jaw sets. He presses the muzzle to his temple and shuts his eyes.

[[SH080 | 2 | EXTREME CLOSE | Locked-off | Sound slams back in]]

Click. The roar of the crowd crashes back in.

[[SH090 | 2 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]

He opens his eyes and stares at the gun. The crowd hits him.

.EXT. CROSSROADS - MOMENTS LATER #S07#

[[SH010 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE, high | Locked-off | Seen from afar (Leonard). His car in frame]]

From far above, the small mob closes around him at the corner of the crossroads. He disappears inside it. Fists and kicks rise and fall. His car stands alone in the middle.

[[SH020 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld | Leonard: rope thrown over the light]]

A rope sails over the arm of a street light at the corner.

[[SH030 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]

They haul him up by the ankles, upside down.

[[SH040 | 3 | CLOSE, upside down | Locked-off | Not exaggerated (Leonard)]]

His face: bruised, a split lip, blood from his ear. With effort, he opens one eye.

[[SH050 | 3 | POV, upside down | Locked-off | Leonard: the shoulder]]

He pulls his arms over his head. A man swings a metal pipe into his shoulder. Again.

[[SH060 | 2 | LOW, looking up | Locked-off | Leonard: from below]]

The pipe rises high against the sky for the last blow.

[[SH070 | 2 | WIDE, high, from above | Locked-off | Leonard: hit in the face. Wide and from behind the man: nothing explicit]]

A crack from the sky. The man with the pipe snaps back and drops. The pipe rings on the asphalt.

[[SH080 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | Method: AI crowd first, simulation only if it fails]]

The crowd steps back from the body, looking up.

.EXT. SKY ABOVE THE TOWN / INT. HELICOPTER - CONTINUOUS #S08#

[[SH010 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | Clancy, hint of Kojima (Leonard, Q12). Airbus ACH160, Lounge cabin (keeps sliding doors; the Exclusive cabin has hinged ones). ASSUMPTION: far enough to stay unheard under the crowd]]

High above and far beyond the rooftops, an Airbus ACH160, glossy and white, holds still in the sky. Its sliding door is open.

[[SH020 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off, cabin vibration | ]]

In the door, between cream leather seats, ROGER, harnessed in, cheek on the stock of a long rifle. He is smiling.

[[SH030 | 4 | SCOPE POV | Steady, stabilized | PROPOSED: the tech that exists but nobody sees]]

The crossroads through his scope. A thin box frames every face: red. One box, upside down under the street light, is green. The crosshair moves from red box to red box.

[[SH040 | 4 | WIDE, from the street, long lens | Locked-off | Distance and dust: nothing explicit]]

Cracks from the sky. People fall. The rest run. Some fall while they run.

[[SH050 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]

Behind Roger, seated, immaculate, a headset over her hair: the BUSINESS LADY.

BUSINESS LADY
That's enough Roger.

[[SH060 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]

Roger's face, for an instant: a child whose candy was taken. Then his face goes blank. He shifts his aim.

[[SH070 | 2 | SCOPE POV | Steady | ]]

The crosshair settles on the rope. A crack.

[[SH080 | 2 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]

The rope snaps.

.EXT. CROSSROADS - CONTINUOUS #S09#

[[SH010 | 5 | MEDIUM | Handheld | Leonard: specify who]]

THE OLD MAN drops onto the asphalt, shoulder first, and screams.

OLD MAN
Fuck! FUCK! Fuck fuck fuck...

He curls up, shaking. A dark stain spreads down his trousers.

[[SH020 | 3 | HIS POV, WIDE | Handheld | Distance: no wounds in frame]]

Bodies lie across the crossroads, certificates stuck to the asphalt between them.

[[SH030 | 5 | MEDIUM, low, his eye height | Locked-off | Leonard: lying back like on a couch, taking it like a champ]]

He rolls onto his back and lies on the sidewalk as if it were a couch, legs out on the street. He catches his breath. He looks at the sky. Nearly a smile.

[[SH040 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | Leonard: angry, repulsed, "fuck you, I won"]]

He props himself up on an elbow, looks at the nearest body with disgust, and spits on it. Hard. Then he holds his stare on it.

[[SH050 | 6 | LOW ANGLE, briefcase in the foreground | Locked-off | Leonard: the helicopter lands as he reaches the case]]

The briefcase lies open in the foreground, seemingly empty. He gets up and limps toward it. Far back, the helicopter comes down into the crossroads beside his car. Its rotor wash blows the certificates across the bodies. He reaches the case.

[[SH060 | 3 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]

He reaches into the pocket inside the lid and takes out a folder.

[[SH070 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]

The BUSINESS LADY steps out, low under the rotors, and walks to him.

[[SH080 | 5 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | His line (Leonard)]]

OLD MAN
What took you so long? I don't pay your ass for nothing.

[[SH090 | 3 | CLOSE, her | Locked-off | Her silence is the answer: its own shot]]

She doesn't answer. She looks at him.

[[SH100 | 4 | TWO SHOT | Locked-off | ]]

She holds out her hand. He gives her the folder. She opens it to the last page.

[[SH110 | 2 | INSERT, the last page | Locked-off | Readable on pause, clear signature. Composited in the edit. PROP: the Agreement (last page of this PDF)]]

Dense clauses. At the bottom, his signature, large and clear.

[[SH120 | 7 | CLOSE | Locked-off | Final line: PROPOSED. Pays off the gas board (S01 SH030) and the empty tank]]

She closes the folder. She looks at the bodies, then at him.

BUSINESS LADY
Now that it's signed, fuel comes down on Monday.
(a beat)
You fixed it.

[[SH130 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]

He holds her look. The corner of his mouth lifts. She turns and walks back to the helicopter. He follows her in.

.INT. HIS CAR - CROSSROADS - CONTINUOUS #S10#

[[SH010 | 10 | MEDIUM, through the windshield | Locked-off | The helicopter going away (Leonard). The bobblehead from his car intro returns]]

The bobblehead in the foreground, hand on its heart, nodding hard in the rotor wash. Through the windshield the helicopter lifts off, banks over the rooftops and goes away into the sky. The bobblehead slows. Keeps nodding. The sky is empty.

> CUT TO BLACK.
